  "term": "catatonia",
  "definition": "Catatonia is a neuropsychiatric disorder marked by abnormal movement, speech, and behavior, such as immobility, mutism, rigid or unusual postures, repetitive movements, echoing speech or actions, or extreme excitement. It can occur with psychiatric conditions or with medical disorders.",
